{"name":"Byzantine Blue","hex":"#006c6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"byzantine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Byzantine ."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A byzant (coin)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/byzantine"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Byzantine blue","blocks":[{"text":"Byzantine blue is a color ranging from light celestial blue or lazuli to dark Egyptian blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Forme_rotonde_e_colori_a_Oia_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Forme_rotonde_e_colori_a_Oia_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_blue","wikidata":"Q40889182"},{"title":"Byzantine Empire","blocks":[{"text":"The Byzantine Empire, also known as the Eastern Roman Empire, was the continuation of the Eastern part of the Roman Empire centred on Constantinople during late antiquity and the Middle Ages. Having survived the fall of the Western Roman Empire in the 5th century AD, it endured until the fall of Constantinople to the Ottoman Empire in 1453. The term 'Byzantine Empire' was coined only after its demise; its citizens used the term 'Roman Empire' and called themselves 'Romans'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Eastern_Roman_Empire_565_CE.svg/330px-Eastern_Roman_Empire_565_CE.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byzantine_Empire","wikidata":"Q12544"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/St._Panteleimon%27s_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG/500px-St._Panteleimon%27s_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/St._Panteleimon%27s_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG/1280px-St._Panteleimon%27s_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/St._Panteleimon%27s_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG/500px-St._Panteleimon%27s_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue of Nerezi (Nebesko plavo)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt._Panteleimon's_Church%2C_Nerezi_14.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Statua_di_Costantino_ai_musei_capitolini.jpg/500px-Statua_di_Costantino_ai_musei_capitolini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=p